# Yespizz implementation workflow

The canonical engineering task queue is `docs/IMPLEMENTATION-BACKLOG.md`.

When asked to continue, complete, or implement the app:

1. Read `docs/PRODUCT.md`, `prd/product-strategy.md`, and
   `docs/IMPLEMENTATION-BACKLOG.md` before editing.
2. Select the first unchecked task whose dependencies are complete unless the user
   names a specific task ID. If several tasks are eligible, prefer **Release blocker**
   over **P0** over **P1**, then document order.
3. Inspect current code and tests before editing; do not reimplement WIP that already
   satisfies acceptance criteria. Documentation can lag implementation.
4. Implement only one task per coherent change/PR.
5. Treat Release blocker and P0 acceptance criteria as mandatory.
6. Preserve the backend invariants: blind provider identity, server-owned pricing and
   dispatch, batch size at most three, and proof-required delivery transitions.
7. Update backend DTOs and `packages/api` DTOs/clients together.
8. Add negative authorization and invalid-transition tests for every privileged or
   state-changing endpoint.
9. Never ship demo coordinates, fake success paths, mock OTPs, raw card collection,
   or local-only chat/call behavior as production functionality.
10. Run targeted checks during development. Run the full Definition of Done
    (`npm ci`, lint, check-types, test, build) before marking Release blockers or
    PLATFORM tasks complete; other tasks require the checks listed on the task plus
    lint/types/tests for touched packages.
11. Mark the task complete only after showing test evidence; record any follow-up as a
    new backlog item instead of silently expanding scope.

## Handoff protocol

When starting work:

1. State the task ID and restate its acceptance criteria.
2. Keep the change scoped to that task and avoid unrelated redesigns.
3. Report changed files, migrations/configuration, test evidence, and remaining risks.
4. Change `[ ]` to `[x]` in the backlog only after every acceptance criterion is verified.

If docs and code disagree, inspect tests and implementation, then update the stale
documentation in the same change.
